  "status_text": "Eight settings can break a light's circuit budget even when any seven fit. Lean checked this for a light that starts on and alternates, with five AND or OR gates and three bit-flipping gates allowed. Every proper selection of those eight settings has a circuit within budget. Lean also checked the general rule for lights fully specified as switches turn on in order. With two-wire gates, any failure appears in an ordered selection no longer than the AND/OR budget plus the number of lights plus two (L-lib-1348, L-lib-1347).",
